  "term": "acute stress disorder",
  "definition": "Acute stress disorder is a mental health condition that develops after a traumatic, often life-threatening event that causes intense fear or horror. It involves dissociation, intrusive memories of the event, avoidance of reminders, and persistent hyperarousal, and it lasts no longer than one month.",
